  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "Brandon Pugh said that not examining how AI helps cyber defense puts one at a huge disadvantage. He described leveraging AI as a national security imperative and said AI requires guardrails to protect consumer privacy and secure data. Pugh stated that findings show many current uses of AI for cyber defense and noted risks, especially in the energy space. In 2023 testimony, he said the U.S.-China rivalry has taken a digital nature and that China has raced with the U.S. on technology including AI.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s3",
    "s4",
    "s5",
    "s6"
   ],
   "sentences": [
    {
